@* ToastRegion's Overview, written by hand after Alert's and Banner's: showing a toast, an action on
   it and toasts after a redirect (each previewed in each mode), the inbox demo, how long they stay
   and where they go, and what an interactive page changes. Accessibility and See also come from
   the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A toast is a short message that appears in a corner of the screen, for news that needs no place on the page, such as "Saved". For a message beside what it's about, use an <Anchor Href="docs/components/alert">Alert</Anchor>.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>Put the ToastRegion in the layout once. <Code>ToastService</Code> then shows toasts in it from anywhere: from a form post on static pages, or from a C# handler on interactive pages. <Code>AddIzzyBlazor()</Code> registers the service.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Showing a toast</Heading>
<TextBlock>To show a toast, call <Code>Success</Code>, <Code>Info</Code>, <Code>Warning</Code> or <Code>Error</Code> on the injected <Code>ToastService</Code>. A title can follow the message.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="toast-region-show" />
<TextBlock>On static pages, the toast renders in the response, so it needs no script. On interactive pages, it's added in the browser at once.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>Show toasts in response to an action, not in <Code>OnInitialized</Code>, which runs twice on a prerendered interactive page.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">An action on the toast</Heading>
<TextBlock>A toast can have an action button, such as Undo or View. Add a <Code>ToastAction</Code>. On static pages, the button follows its <Code>Href</Code>; on interactive pages, its <Code>OnClick</Code> runs C#.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="toast-region-undo" />
<TextBlock>Static pages have no connection to run C# over, so a toast shown there requires an <Code>Href</Code>. A toast action with only <Code>OnClick</Code> throws on static pages.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">After a redirect</Heading>
<TextBlock>A toast can follow the user to the next page after a form post, so post-redirect-get works. In the form post's handler, show the toast before calling <Code>NavigateTo</Code>. The toast travels to the next page in a short-lived cookie.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="toast-region-redirect" />
<TextBlock>On interactive pages, the toast goes to the browser at once, before <Code>NavigateTo</Code> loads the next page, and it stays on screen as the page changes. <Code>forceLoad</Code> loads a whole new page, which loses the toast; show it from the page you land on instead.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>This inbox posts each Archive, then redirects with the archived ids in the URL. Its Undo is a link back to the URL without that conversation:</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="toast-region-inbox" WidthSwitch />

<Heading Level="2">How long it stays</Heading>
<TextBlock>Toasts stay for 5000 milliseconds by default. To change that for every toast, set <Code>Duration</Code> on the region; <Code>0</Code> keeps toasts open. To change it for one toast, set that toast's own <Code>Duration</Code>.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Durations</Code>
<List Gap="2">
    <ListItem>By default, an error stays until the user closes it.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>A toast with an action stays twice as long.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>With <Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">JavaScript off</Anchor>, no toast closes by itself. Each stays until the user clicks its close button, or the next page loads.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">Where they go</Heading>
<TextBlock>Toasts stack in the bottom end corner by default. To stack them in another corner or edge, set <Code>Placement</Code>: <Code>TopStart</Code>, <Code>TopCenter</Code>, <Code>TopEnd</Code>, <Code>BottomStart</Code>, <Code>BottomCenter</Code> or <Code>BottomEnd</Code>. To change how they look, set <Code>Variant</Code>, which styles them as alerts are styled; the default, <Code>Outline</Code>, is a raised card.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and localization</Heading>
<TextBlock>The region's name is <Code>Label</Code>, "Notifications" by default. The close buttons' name is <Code>DismissLabel</Code>, "Dismiss" by default. You can also set them for the whole app as in <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">Text and other languages</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        @* MainLayout.razor, once for the app *@
        <ToastRegion />

        @* A page *@
        @inject ToastService Toasts

        <form method="post" @formname="save" @onsubmit="Save">
            <AntiforgeryToken />
            <Button Submit>Save</Button>
        </form>

        @code {
            private void Save() => Toasts.Success("Your changes are live.", "Saved");
        }
        """;

    private const string Durations = """
        @* Toasts stay 8 seconds, 16 with an action; errors stay until closed. *@
        <ToastRegion Duration="8000" />

        @* This one stays until it's closed. *@
        Toasts.Show(new ToastMessage("Export ready.", Status.Success, Duration: 0,
            Action: new("Download", Href: "/exports/42")));
        """;
}
